<title>USA: SkyMall Inc Q1 shr rises.</title>
<headline>SkyMall Inc Q1 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>SkyMall Inc.</p>
<p>		     Summary Financial and Operating Data</p>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except share, per-share and operating data)</p>
<p>					     For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							 1997	   1996</p>
<p>Statements of Operations Data:</p>
<p> Merchandise sales, net		 $	8,084 $	5,882</p>
<p> Placement fees and other			3,507	  3,073</p>
<p>    Total revenues				11,591	  8,955</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold				6,610	  4,696</p>
<p>    Gross margin				   4,981	  4,259</p>
<p> Total operating expenses			4,638	  3,875</p>
<p> Income from operations			    343	    384</p>
<p> Interest income (expense) and other, net     84	  (171)</p>
<p> Income before provision for income taxes    427	    213</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			 --	     --</p>
<p>    Net income					 427	    213</p>
<p> Net income per common share		    0.05	   0.04</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   8,818,016    5,150,000</p>
<p>Operating Data:</p>
<p>Number of domestic enplanements (a)(b)</p>
<p>						 135,649,000  127,554,000</p>
<p> Domestic enplanement percentage (b)(c)	69%	    58%</p>
<p> Revenue per passenger enplanement (b)(d)  0.086	  0.080</p>
<p>(a) Represents the number of revenue passengers flown on scheduled domestic airlines in the given period. (b) Enplanement information has been estimated based on historical enplanement data. (c) Represents the passenger enplanements on domestic airlines that carried the SkyMall catalog during the period as a percentage of total domestic passenger enplanements in the period by all scheduled domestic airlines. (d) Revenue per passenger enplanement is net merchandise sales for the period divided by the number of domestic enplanements for the period on all scheduled domestic airlines that carried the SkyMall catalog.</p>
